 ### [Slice-based Volume Rendering using Pixel Bender](5445-slice-based-volume-rendering-using-pixel-bender.md)
-Uses view-aligned slices and a static 3D texture via Pixel Bender shaders. Renders volume data directly without isosurface extraction, allowing translucent cross-sections.
+A real-time volume rendering technique that uses view-aligned slices and a static 3D texture (set of cross sections), implemented via Pixel Bender shaders. It differs from surface rendering methods (e.g., marching cubes) by rendering volume data directly without building an isosurface, allowing for translucent cross-sections.
 
